  "variants": {
    "fp32": "comfy.sd.VAE(dtype=float32), the ComfyUI default on this CPU",
    "bf16": "comfy.sd.VAE(dtype=bfloat16), what --bf16-vae selects",
    "fp32-cl / bf16-cl": "plus Conv3d/Conv2d weights in channels_last(_3d) and a channels_last_3d decoder input",
    "fp32-clfix / bf16-clfix": "plus an nn.Upsample forward wrapper that restrides a channels_last N=1 input to (c*h*w, 1, w*c, c) with as_strided (zero copy, same values)"
  },
  "code_path_findings": [
    "WanVAE.decode of a single-frame latent runs without feat_cache, so every CausalConv3d takes the causal_zero path in comfy/ops.py: the weight is sliced to the input depth (kd=1) and conv3d runs on a 1-frame input",
    "Resample rearranges b c t h w -> (b t) c h w for nn.Upsample(nearest-exact) and Conv2d; with T=1 and a channels_last_3d tensor the size-1 batch dimension keeps the channel stride (384 or 192), so suggest_memory_format() reports contiguous and the upsample allocates an NCHW output",
    "RMS_norm is F.normalize(x, dim=1) * scale * gamma; its channel reduction (linalg_vector_norm) is strided in NCDHW and contiguous in channels_last"
  ],
