  "limitations": [
    "One machine, one 512x512 single-frame latent shape, ten torch threads; other resolutions, thread counts or video latents were not measured",
    "The end-to-end figures cover the warmed sampler and VAE decode in one process; model loading, text encoding and image saving are excluded",
    "Eight runs per variant with all paired deltas negative; no statistical test was run",
    "Absolute decode times differ between processes and residency (bf16-clfix: 1.22 s median in the harness with two VAEs resident, 1.62 s in the standalone A/B with four, 1.30-1.41 s standalone warm decodes); compare variants only inside one run",
    "BF16 output differs from the FP32 VAE (PSNR 46.8-49.2 dB, about 23% of pixels differ by at least one level); differences concentrate in high-frequency detail. No perceptual or quality-equivalence claim is made",
    "The clfix wrapper assumes N=1 after the (b t) rearrange; batched or multi-frame decodes need a general stride check",
    "Production would need --bf16-vae (a launch-flag change needing approval) and a node-side patch for the channels_last/restride part; neither is deployed"
  ],
